<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Concentration Inequalities</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We record a few standard concentration inequalities that will be used throughout. For background, we refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Concentration inequalities)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},\dots,Z_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},\dots,Z_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. random variables and define the empirical mean <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Z}\coloneqq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Z}\coloneqq\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Hoeffding) If </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}\in\mathinner{\left[a,b\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}\in\mathinner{\left[a,b\right]}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\bar{Z}-\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[Z_{1}\right]}\right\rvert}\leq\mathinner{\left(b-a\right)}\sqrt{\frac{1}{2T}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}}\right)}\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\bar{Z}-\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[Z_{1}\right]}\right\rvert}\leq\mathinner{\left(b-a\right)}\sqrt{\frac{1}{2T}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}}\right)}\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Bernstein) If </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert Z_{1}-\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[Z_{1}\right]}\right\rvert}\leq b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert Z_{1}-\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[Z_{1}\right]}\right\rvert}\leq b</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\bar{Z}-\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[Z_{1}\right]}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{2b}{3T}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}+\sqrt{\frac{2\Var\mathinner{\left(Z_{1}\right)}}{T}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}}\right)}\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\bar{Z}-\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[Z_{1}\right]}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{2b}{3T}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}+\sqrt{\frac{2\Var\mathinner{\left(Z_{1}\right)}}{T}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}}\right)}\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Learning under Massart Noise</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be a distribution over <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\coloneqq P\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}\leq\eta&lt;\frac{1}{2}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\coloneqq P\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}\leq\eta&lt;\frac{1}{2}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathcal{X}\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathcal{X}\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the Massart noise condition with rate <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the Bayes error by <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{*}\coloneqq P\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{*}\coloneqq P\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The following result characterizes the pointwise error of a classifier in terms of <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathcal{X}\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathcal{X}\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}-\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}=\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}-\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}=\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ Appendix B Learning under Massart Noise ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This follows from</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}=f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}+\mathinner{\left(1-\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}=f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}+\mathinner{\left(1-\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\mathinner{\left(1-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}\right)}+\mathinner{\left(1-\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\mathinner{\left(1-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}\right)}+\mathinner{\left(1-\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}+\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}+\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right)}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The bounded noise assumption implies that <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\geq 1-2\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\eta^{*}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\geq 1-2\eta</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, if we integrate the equality of <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ Appendix B Learning under Massart Noise ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> with respect to marginal <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and rearrange, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\right)}\leq\frac{P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}-\eta^{*}}{1-2\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\right)}\leq\frac{P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}-\eta^{*}}{1-2\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The key idea behind the Massart fast rate is that we can bound the following variance:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Var_{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Var_{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{P}\mathinner{\left[\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}\right\rvert}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{P}\mathinner{\left[\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}\right\rvert}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}-\eta^{*}}{1-2\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{P\mathinner{\left(f\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}-\eta^{*}}{1-2\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Suppose that we are trying to learn a finite function class <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(X_{t},Y_{t}\right)}_{t=1}^{T}\overset{iid}{\sim}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(X_{t},Y_{t}\right)}_{t=1}^{T}\overset{iid}{\sim}P</annotation></semantics></math> be a sample and consider the empirical minimizer</p>
<table id="A2.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{f}\in\argmin_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\mathinner{\left\{\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X_{t}\right)}\neq Y_{t}\right\}}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{f}\in\argmin_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\mathinner{\left\{\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X_{t}\right)}\neq Y_{t}\right\}}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Applying Bernstein’s inequality on random variables <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X_{t}\right)}\neq Y_{t}\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X_{t}\right)}\neq Y_{t}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f\mathinner{\left(X_{t}\right)}\neq Y_{t}\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X_{t}\right)}\neq Y_{t}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math> and taking a union bound over <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can conclude that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(\hat{f}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}-\eta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P\mathinner{\left(\hat{f}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}-\eta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathcal{F}\right\rvert}/\delta\right)}}{n\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathcal{F}\right\rvert}/\delta\right)}}{n\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">In other words, <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-optimal provided that <math id="A2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\gtrsim\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathcal{F}\right\rvert}/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≳</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\gtrsim\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathcal{F}\right\rvert}/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To extend this idea to general VC classes, we refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs of <a href="#S3" title="3 MDL Upper Bounds ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Statistical Learning ‣ 3 MDL Upper Bounds ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the mixture also satisfies the bounded noise assumption:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\middle|X=x\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\middle|X=x\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathcal{U}}\alpha_{i}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}P_{i}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\middle|X=x\right)}\leq\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i\in\mathcal{U}}\alpha_{i}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}P_{i}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\middle|X=x\right)}\leq\eta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}\coloneqq\frac{p_{i}^{X}}{\sum_{j}p_{j}^{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}\coloneqq\frac{p_{i}^{X}}{\sum_{j}p_{j}^{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is the density of the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-marginal of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to some dominating measure. Then, the ERM solution <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\epsilon,\delta\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖲𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\epsilon,\delta\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> samples from <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}\mathinner{\left(\hat{f}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}\leq\epsilon+\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}=\epsilon+\frac{1}{\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathcal{U}\right\rvert}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{U}}\eta_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}\mathinner{\left(\hat{f}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}\leq\epsilon+\bar{P}_{\mathcal{U}}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right)}=\epsilon+\frac{1}{\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\mathcal{U}\right\rvert}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{U}}\eta_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with probability <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ 3.2 Testing ‣ 3 MDL Upper Bounds ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For convenience, let us rewrite the sample size lower bound as <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}\geq 2\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}\frac{\epsilon/8+\nu}{\mathinner{\left(\epsilon/8\right)}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}\geq 2\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{2}{\delta}\right)}\frac{\epsilon/8+\nu}{\mathinner{\left(\epsilon/8\right)}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Bernstein’s inequality, we know that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\sqrt{\frac{2\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}\log\mathinner{\left(2/\delta\right)}}{\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}}+\frac{2\log\mathinner{\left(2/\delta\right)}}{\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}+\frac{\epsilon}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\sqrt{\frac{2\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}\log\mathinner{\left(2/\delta\right)}}{\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}}+\frac{2\log\mathinner{\left(2/\delta\right)}}{\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}+\frac{\epsilon}{8}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with probability <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}\leq\epsilon/8+\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}\leq\epsilon/8+\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}+\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}+\frac{\epsilon}{8}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{2}+\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}+\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}+\frac{\epsilon}{8}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{2}+\nu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Now, suppose that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}&gt;\epsilon+\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}&gt;\epsilon+\nu</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\mathinner{\left(p\right)}\coloneqq p-a\sqrt{\frac{p}{a+b}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\mathinner{\left(p\right)}\coloneqq p-a\sqrt{\frac{p}{a+b}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}\mathinner{\left(p\right)}=1-\frac{a}{2\sqrt{p\mathinner{\left(a+b\right)}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}\mathinner{\left(p\right)}=1-\frac{a}{2\sqrt{p\mathinner{\left(a+b\right)}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing for <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leq 2\sqrt{p\mathinner{\left(a+b\right)}}\iff p\geq\frac{a^{2}}{4\mathinner{\left(a+b\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leq 2\sqrt{p\mathinner{\left(a+b\right)}}\iff p\geq\frac{a^{2}}{4\mathinner{\left(a+b\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specializing to <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\epsilon+\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\epsilon+\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\epsilon/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\epsilon/8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that this condition is clearly ensured:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon+\nu\geq\frac{\epsilon}{8}&gt;\frac{\mathinner{\left(\epsilon/8\right)}^{2}}{4\mathinner{\left(\epsilon/8+\nu\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon+\nu\geq\frac{\epsilon}{8}&gt;\frac{\mathinner{\left(\epsilon/8\right)}^{2}}{4\mathinner{\left(\epsilon/8+\nu\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}&gt;\epsilon+\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}&gt;\epsilon+\nu</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption, we can again apply Bernstein to obtain</p>
<table id="A3.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}-\frac{\epsilon}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}-\frac{\epsilon}{8}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\epsilon+\nu-\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+\nu}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}-\frac{\epsilon}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\epsilon+\nu-\frac{\epsilon}{8}\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+\nu}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}-\frac{\epsilon}{8}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\frac{\epsilon}{2}+\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\frac{\epsilon}{2}+\nu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where we used the fact that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+\nu}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}\leq\sqrt{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon+\nu}{\epsilon/8+\nu}}\leq\sqrt{8}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7/8-1/\sqrt{8}&gt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mn>8</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7/8-1/\sqrt{8}&gt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3 (() upper bound). ‣ 3.3 () Upper Bound ‣ 3 MDL Upper Bounds ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the reasoning above, we know that we succeed with probability <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> under the specified parameters. Since we learn at least half of the distributions on every round, we only require <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\left\lceil\log_{2}k\right\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\left\lceil\log_{2}k\right\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> rounds. On every round, ERM requires <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\frac{\epsilon}{16},\frac{\delta}{2T}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖲𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\frac{\epsilon}{16},\frac{\delta}{2T}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> samples. For testing, each <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled at most <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathsf{T}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{i},\epsilon,\frac{\delta}{2kT}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathsf{T}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{i},\epsilon,\frac{\delta}{2kT}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> times on every round. Hence, the total sample size required is</p>
<table id="A3.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{RCN}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{1\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}k},\epsilon,\delta\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖱𝖢𝖭</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{RCN}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{1\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}k},\epsilon,\delta\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq T\mathinner{\left(T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\frac{\epsilon}{16},\frac{\delta}{2T}\right)}+\sum_{i=1}^{k}T_{\mathsf{T}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{i},\epsilon,\frac{\delta}{2kT}\right)}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖲𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq T\mathinner{\left(T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\frac{\epsilon}{16},\frac{\delta}{2T}\right)}+\sum_{i=1}^{k}T_{\mathsf{T}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{i},\epsilon,\frac{\delta}{2kT}\right)}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\mathinner{\left(\log k\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d\log\mathinner{\left(1/\epsilon\right)}+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log k}{\delta}\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{k}{\delta}\right)}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{\epsilon+\eta_{i}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\mathinner{\left(\log k\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d\log\mathinner{\left(1/\epsilon\right)}+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log k}{\delta}\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{k}{\delta}\right)}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{\epsilon+\eta_{i}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log^{2}\mathinner{\left(\frac{k}{\delta}\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d\log\mathinner{\left(1/\epsilon\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{\epsilon+\eta_{i}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log^{2}\mathinner{\left(\frac{k}{\delta}\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d\log\mathinner{\left(1/\epsilon\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{\epsilon+\eta_{i}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4 (() upper bound). ‣ 3.4 () Upper Bound ‣ 3 MDL Upper Bounds ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the description of the procedure, and by tuning <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> appropriately, we know that we can guarantee success with probability at least <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, we learn half of the distributions on every round, so that <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\left\lceil\log_{2}k\right\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\left\lceil\log_{2}k\right\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> rounds suffices. On each round, ERM uses</p>
<table id="A3.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\frac{\epsilon}{32},\frac{\delta}{2T}\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{d+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log k}{\delta}\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖲𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\eta,\frac{\epsilon}{32},\frac{\delta}{2T}\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{d+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log k}{\delta}\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">samples, and testing requires at most</p>
<table id="A3.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{T}}\mathinner{\left(\eta^{*}+\frac{\epsilon}{2},\frac{\epsilon}{2},\frac{\delta}{4\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}kT}\right)}=32\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{8\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}kT}{\delta}\right)}\frac{9\epsilon+16\eta^{*}}{\epsilon^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{T}}\mathinner{\left(\eta^{*}+\frac{\epsilon}{2},\frac{\epsilon}{2},\frac{\delta}{4\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}kT}\right)}=32\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{8\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}kT}{\delta}\right)}\frac{9\epsilon+16\eta^{*}}{\epsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">samples per distribution. Putting these together, we obtain a total sample complexity upper bound of</p>
<table id="A3.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{MM}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{1\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}k}^{*},\eta_{1\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}k},\epsilon,\delta\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝖬𝖬</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{MM}}\mathinner{\left(\eta_{1\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}k}^{*},\eta_{1\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}k},\epsilon,\delta\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex89.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\mathinner{\left(\log k\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log k}{\delta}\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}k}{\delta}\right)}\frac{k\mathinner{\left(\epsilon+\eta^{*}\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\mathinner{\left(\log k\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log k}{\delta}\right)}}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}k}{\delta}\right)}\frac{k\mathinner{\left(\epsilon+\eta^{*}\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\log^{2}\mathinner{\left(\frac{\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}k}{\delta}\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\frac{k\mathinner{\left(\epsilon+\eta^{*}\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\log^{2}\mathinner{\left(\frac{\mathinner{\left(\eta/\epsilon+1\right)}k}{\delta}\right)}\mathinner{\left(\frac{d}{\epsilon\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}}+\frac{k\mathinner{\left(\epsilon+\eta^{*}\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs of <a href="#S4" title="4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Testing via empirical errors). ‣ Agnostic Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hoeffding’s inequality tells us that, with probability at least <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(2/\delta\right)}}{2\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\sqrt{\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(2/\delta\right)}}{2\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{12}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Under this high-probability event, we immediately obtain our claim:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}\leq\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}\leq\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex92.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}\leq\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}+\frac{\epsilon}{12}\leq\frac{1}{4}+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}\leq\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}+\frac{\epsilon}{12}\leq\frac{1}{4}+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}&gt;\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}&gt;\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}&gt;\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}-\frac{\epsilon}{12}=\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Longrightarrow\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}&gt;\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{6}-\frac{\epsilon}{12}=\frac{1}{4}+\frac{\epsilon}{12}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (From learning to testing). ‣ Learning-Augmented Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Learning under Massart Noise ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, we know that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Var_{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{g\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}\right)}\leq\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}}{1-2\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>f</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Var_{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{g\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}-\mathbb{I}\mathinner{\left\{f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y\right\}}\right)}\leq\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}}{1-2\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for any function <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathcal{X}\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\mathcal{X}\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Bernstein’s inequality then tells us that, with probability <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta/3</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}-\mathinner{\left(\emperr\mathinner{\left(g;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right)}\right\rvert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}-\mathinner{\left(\emperr\mathinner{\left(g;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right)}\right\rvert}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{3\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{6}{\delta}\right)}+\sqrt{\frac{2\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}}{\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{6}{\delta}\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{3\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{6}{\delta}\right)}+\sqrt{\frac{2\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}}{\mathinner{\left(1-2\eta\right)}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert S\right\rvert}}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{6}{\delta}\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\epsilon}{48}+\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon}{48}\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\epsilon}{48}+\sqrt{\frac{\epsilon}{48}\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{96}+\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{96}+\frac{\err\mathinner{\left(g;P\right)}-\eta^{*}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where we used AM-GM in the last inequality. Since <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, we can then conclude that <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are close in empirical error: with probability <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-2\delta/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-2\delta/3</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{96}+\frac{3}{2}\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{48}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{96}+\frac{3}{2}\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{48}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let us take a union bound of this event with the Bernstein bound above on our function of interest <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, so that they simultaneously occur with probability <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this event, we then have that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}+\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{19\epsilon}{48}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="3.128em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>19</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}+\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{19\epsilon}{48}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{48}+2\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{41\epsilon}{48}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="3.128em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{48}+2\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{41\epsilon}{48}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\leq\frac{\epsilon}{12}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{96}+\frac{3}{2}\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}\leq\frac{5\epsilon}{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="3.128em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>32</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{3\epsilon}{96}+\frac{3}{2}\mathinner{\left(\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}-\eta^{*}\right)}\leq\frac{5\epsilon}{32}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}+\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{21\epsilon}{96}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="3.128em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>err</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>21</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mn>96</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 28.45274pt\Longrightarrow\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f;S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}\right\rvert}+\mathinner{\!\left\lvert\emperr\mathinner{\left(f^{*};S\right)}-\emperr\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};S\right)}\right\rvert}\leq\frac{21\epsilon}{96}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (() upper bound). ‣ Learning-Augmented Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1/\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1/\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Testing via empirical errors). ‣ Agnostic Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> immediately implies correctness of the decision, and the sample size is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{C}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,\delta\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(1/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{C}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,\delta\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{\log\mathinner{\left(1/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, suppose that <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;1/\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;1/\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(1/4,\epsilon/48,\delta/3\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖲𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(1/4,\epsilon/48,\delta/3\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> samples, we know that ERM guarantees <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};P\right)}\leq 1/4+\epsilon/48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(\hat{f};P\right)}\leq 1/4+\epsilon/48</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/3</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, correctness of our decision follows from <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (From learning to testing). ‣ Learning-Augmented Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. In this case, the sample size obtained is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\frac{\epsilon}{48},\frac{\delta}{3}\right)}+T_{\mathsf{L}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\epsilon,\delta\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{d}{\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖲𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\frac{\epsilon}{48},\frac{\delta}{3}\right)}+T_{\mathsf{L}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\epsilon,\delta\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{d}{\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{\delta}\right)}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Combining both conditions yields the desired sample complexity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4 (() lower bound). ‣ 4.2 () Lower Bound ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the hardness of (<a href="#S4.Ex32" title="Equation SHT ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">SHT</span></a>), we first construct a preliminary base testing problem and establish a lower bound for it.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\mathinner{\left(0,1\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\mathinner{\left(0,1\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\epsilon\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\epsilon\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Define a random variable <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> with PMF</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{X}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}=\begin{cases}1-d\epsilon,&amp;x=0\\
\epsilon/d,&amp;x\in\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{X}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}=\begin{cases}1-d\epsilon,&amp;x=0\\
\epsilon/d,&amp;x\in\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In addition, let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket\to\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math> be an underlying function, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}=1/4\quad\forall x\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}=1/4\quad\forall x\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We sample i.i.d. pairs <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> and must ensure that:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A4.Ex109X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex109X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{$H_{0}$: If $f^{*}=f_{0}$, output $\mathsf{YES}$ with probability at least $3/4$.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">: If </mtext><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">, output </mtext><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> with probability at least </mtext><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{$H_{0}$: If $f^{*}=f_{0}$, output $\mathsf{YES}$ with probability at least $3/4$.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(SHT-Base)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.Ex109Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex109Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{$H_{1}$: If $f^{*}$ equals $1$ precisely on a size-$d$ subset, output $\mathsf{NO}$ with probability at least $3/4$.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">: If </mtext><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> equals </mtext><mn>1</mn><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> precisely on a size-</mtext><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> subset, output </mtext><mi>𝖭𝖮</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> with probability at least </mtext><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{$H_{1}$: If $f^{*}$ equals $1$ precisely on a size-$d$ subset, output $\mathsf{NO}$ with probability at least $3/4$.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This problem requires a sample size of</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T\geq\frac{3d}{4\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(1+\log 2\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T\geq\frac{3d}{4\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(1+\log 2\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be the joint distribution over <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(X_{t},Y_{t}\right)}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(X_{t},Y_{t}\right)}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and, similarly, <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{R}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{R}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> the joint under <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and subset <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\subset\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\subset\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. We also use lower-case <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the corresponding PMFs. With abuse of notation, let <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{YES}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{YES}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{NO}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖭𝖮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{NO}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event that a successful algorithm outputs each decision. Let <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be chosen uniformly at random from all subsets of size <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. The learner must ensure that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{3}{2}\leq P_{0}^{T}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{YES}\right)}+\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{NO}\right)}\right]}\leq 1+\TV\mathinner{\left(P_{0}^{T},\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝖭𝖮</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{3}{2}\leq P_{0}^{T}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{YES}\right)}+\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{NO}\right)}\right]}\leq 1+\TV\mathinner{\left(P_{0}^{T},\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">In other words, we need</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\TV\mathinner{\left(P_{0}^{T},\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\right)}\geq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\TV\mathinner{\left(P_{0}^{T},\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\right)}\geq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">To upper bound the TV distance, we will work with the <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence and apply Ingster’s method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\chi^{2}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\middle\|P_{0}^{T}\right)}+1=\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[G^{T}\mathinner{\left(R,R^{\prime}\right)}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\chi^{2}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\middle\|P_{0}^{T}\right)}+1=\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[G^{T}\mathinner{\left(R,R^{\prime}\right)}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. subsets and</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G\mathinner{\left(R,R^{\prime}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G\mathinner{\left(R,R^{\prime}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex114.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}\sim P_{0}}\mathinner{\left[\frac{p_{R}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}{p_{0}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}\cdot\frac{p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}{p_{0}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}\sim P_{0}}\mathinner{\left[\frac{p_{R}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}{p_{0}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}\cdot\frac{p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}{p_{0}\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket}p_{0}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\sum_{y\in\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}}\frac{p_{R}\mathinner{\left(y|x\right)}p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(y|x\right)}}{p_{0}\mathinner{\left(y|x\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket}p_{0}\mathinner{\left(x\right)}\sum_{y\in\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}}\frac{p_{R}\mathinner{\left(y|x\right)}p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(y|x\right)}}{p_{0}\mathinner{\left(y|x\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-d\epsilon+\frac{\epsilon}{d}\sum_{x\in\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}}\underbrace{\mathinner{\left[\frac{4}{3}p_{R}\mathinner{\left(0|x\right)}p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(0|x\right)}+4p_{R}\mathinner{\left(1|x\right)}p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(1|x\right)}\right]}}_{\eqqcolon\mathinner{\left(\star\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-d\epsilon+\frac{\epsilon}{d}\sum_{x\in\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}}\underbrace{\mathinner{\left[\frac{4}{3}p_{R}\mathinner{\left(0|x\right)}p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(0|x\right)}+4p_{R}\mathinner{\left(1|x\right)}p_{R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left(1|x\right)}\right]}}_{\eqqcolon\mathinner{\left(\star\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">To evaluate this sum, let us consider two possibilities:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\notin R\cap R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\notin R\cap R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, at least one of the conditional PMFs will be <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ber\mathinner{\left(1/4\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ber\mathinner{\left(1/4\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the other one be <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Ber\mathinner{\left(q\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Ber\mathinner{\left(q\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathinner{\left(\star\right)}=\frac{4}{3}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\mathinner{\left(1-p\right)}+4\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot p=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathinner{\left(\star\right)}=\frac{4}{3}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\mathinner{\left(1-p\right)}+4\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot p=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in R\cap R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in R\cap R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathinner{\left(\star\right)}=\frac{4}{3}\cdot\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4}\right)}^{2}+4\cdot\mathinner{\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)}^{2}=\frac{7}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathinner{\left(\star\right)}=\frac{4}{3}\cdot\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4}\right)}^{2}+4\cdot\mathinner{\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)}^{2}=\frac{7}{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">As a result, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G\mathinner{\left(R,R^{\prime}\right)}=1-d\epsilon+\frac{\epsilon}{d}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}-\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}+\frac{7}{3}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}=1+\frac{4\epsilon}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G\mathinner{\left(R,R^{\prime}\right)}=1-d\epsilon+\frac{\epsilon}{d}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}-\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}+\frac{7}{3}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}=1+\frac{4\epsilon}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging this back into the <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> formula yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\chi^{2}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\middle\|P_{0}^{T}\right)}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\chi^{2}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\middle\|P_{0}^{T}\right)}+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex120.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\mathinner{\left(1+\frac{4\epsilon}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}^{T}\right]}\leq\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\frac{4\epsilon T}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\mathinner{\left(1+\frac{4\epsilon}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}^{T}\right]}\leq\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\frac{4\epsilon T}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we observe that the random variable <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a hypergeometric distribution: conditioned on <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, we can see <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}</annotation></semantics></math> as the number of “successes” when we draw <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R^{\prime}\right\rvert}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R^{\prime}\right\rvert}=d</annotation></semantics></math> times without replacement from a population of size <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> that contains exactly <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\right\rvert}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\right\rvert}=d</annotation></semantics></math> successes. That is, <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}|R\sim\HG\mathinner{\left(N=d^{2},K=d,n=d\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>HG</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}|R\sim\HG\mathinner{\left(N=d^{2},K=d,n=d\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\sim\HG\mathinner{\left(N=d^{2},K=d,n=d\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>HG</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\sim\HG\mathinner{\left(N=d^{2},K=d,n=d\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is then to bound the MGF of this hypergeometric, which is smaller than the MGF of its binomial counterpart:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\lambda\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\lambda\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex121.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\lambda\Bin\mathinner{\left(n=d,p=1/d\right)}\right)}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\lambda\Bin\mathinner{\left(n=d,p=1/d\right)}\right)}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathinner{\left(1-\frac{1}{d}+\frac{e^{\lambda}}{d}\right)}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathinner{\left(1-\frac{1}{d}+\frac{e^{\lambda}}{d}\right)}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\mathinner{\left(d\log\mathinner{\left(1+\frac{e^{\lambda}-1}{d}\right)}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\mathinner{\left(d\log\mathinner{\left(1+\frac{e^{\lambda}-1}{d}\right)}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\mathinner{\left(e^{\lambda}-1\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\mathinner{\left(e^{\lambda}-1\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we can combine everything to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\TV\mathinner{\left(P_{0}^{T},\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\TV\mathinner{\left(P_{0}^{T},\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex125.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\chi^{2}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\middle\|P_{0}^{T}\right)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\chi^{2}\mathinner{\left(\mathbb{E}_{R}\mathinner{\left[P_{R}^{T}\right]}\middle\|P_{0}^{T}\right)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\frac{4\epsilon T}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}\right]}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{R,R^{\prime}}\mathinner{\left[\exp\mathinner{\left(\frac{4\epsilon T}{3d}\mathinner{\!\left\lvert R\cap R^{\prime}\right\rvert}\right)}\right]}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\exp\mathinner{\left(\exp\mathinner{\left(\frac{4\epsilon T}{3d}\right)}-1\right)}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{\exp\mathinner{\left(\exp\mathinner{\left(\frac{4\epsilon T}{3d}\right)}-1\right)}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Since the TV distance has to be larger than <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we can then conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T\geq\frac{3d}{4\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(1+\log 2\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T\geq\frac{3d}{4\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(1+\log 2\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremarkx3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremarkx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark</span></span><span id="Thmremarkx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(External randomness)<span id="Thmremarkx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremarkx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremarkx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The lower bound of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> still applies when the learner has access to an external source of randomness; i.e., it applies to randomized learners.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can readily prove our original claim using <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. Suppose that <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq\frac{1}{2\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq\frac{1}{2\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}\subset\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}^{\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}\subset\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}^{\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket}</annotation></semantics></math> be the class of <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> along with all functions <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> that equal <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> precisely on a subset <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\subset\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\subset\mathinner{\left[d^{2}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\VC\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{F}\right)}=d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>VCdim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\VC\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{F}\right)}=d</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be an (<a href="#S4.Ex32" title="Equation SHT ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">SHT</span></a>) algorithm with sample complexity <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathcal{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathcal{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will construct a learner for (<a href="#A4.Ex109" title="Equation SHT-Base ‣ Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">SHT-Base</span></a>) with parameters <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(d,2\epsilon\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(d,2\epsilon\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. To that end, let our data-generating distribution <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be according to one of the hypotheses, and suppose that <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> wishes to test if <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-optimal. Its error is given by <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}=\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(Y=1\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}=\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(Y=1\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that we can make the following observations:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and, thus, <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}=1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}=1/4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and subset <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, the functions <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> disagree precisely on <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}=\mathinner{\left(1-2d\epsilon\right)}\cdot\frac{1}{4}+\mathinner{\left(d^{2}-d\right)}\cdot\frac{2\epsilon}{d}\cdot\frac{1}{4}+d\cdot\frac{2\epsilon}{d}\cdot\frac{3}{4}=\frac{1}{4}+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\err\mathinner{\left(f;P\right)}=\mathinner{\left(1-2d\epsilon\right)}\cdot\frac{1}{4}+\mathinner{\left(d^{2}-d\right)}\cdot\frac{2\epsilon}{d}\cdot\frac{1}{4}+d\cdot\frac{2\epsilon}{d}\cdot\frac{3}{4}=\frac{1}{4}+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, if we run <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathcal{A}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,1/4\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathcal{A}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,1/4\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> samples, we output <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{YES}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{YES}</annotation></semantics></math> precisely under <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3/4</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, we are able to distinguish <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The lower bound of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> then implies that <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> requires a sample size of at least</p>
<table id="A4.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathcal{A}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,1/4\right)}\geq\frac{3d}{8\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(1+\log 2\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathcal{A}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,1/4\right)}\geq\frac{3d}{8\epsilon}\log\mathinner{\left(1+\log 2\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 4.5 (() upper bound). ‣ 4.3 Multi-Distribution SHT ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This proof is the natural extension of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 4.3 (() upper bound). ‣ Learning-Augmented Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> to multiple distributions. Note that we do not require any union bounds due to the objective. When <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 1/\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 1/\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we similarly apply <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Testing via empirical errors). ‣ Agnostic Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> to conclude correctness. The sample size is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k\cdot T_{\mathsf{C}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,\delta\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{k\log\mathinner{\left(1/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖢</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k\cdot T_{\mathsf{C}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,\delta\right)}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{k\log\mathinner{\left(1/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;1/\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;1/\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (From learning to testing). ‣ Learning-Augmented Testing. ‣ 4.1 () Upper Bounds ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> along with a union bound over <math id="A4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}</annotation></semantics></math> again ensures correctness, with a sample size of</p>
<table id="A4.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k\mathinner{\left[T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\frac{\epsilon}{48},\frac{\delta}{3}\right)}+T_{\mathsf{L}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\epsilon,\delta\right)}\right]}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{kd\log\mathinner{\left(1/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖲𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝖫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k\mathinner{\left[T_{\mathsf{SL}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\frac{\epsilon}{48},\frac{\delta}{3}\right)}+T_{\mathsf{L}}\mathinner{\left(\frac{1}{4},\epsilon,\delta\right)}\right]}=O\mathinner{\left(\frac{kd\log\mathinner{\left(1/\delta\right)}}{\epsilon}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 4.6 (Multi-Distribution SHT lower bound). ‣ 4.3 Multi-Distribution SHT ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the next result, we construct an (<a href="#S4.Ex46" title="Equation MSHT ‣ 4.3 Multi-Distribution SHT ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">MSHT</span></a>) instance that suffers from the <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\mathinner{\left(kd/\epsilon\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\mathinner{\left(kd/\epsilon\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound when <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq\frac{1}{2\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq\frac{1}{2\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby proving our desired hardness claim.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in\mathinner{\left(0,1\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in\mathinner{\left(0,1\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> be such that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 8\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 8\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d\epsilon\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d\epsilon\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Define covariate space <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\coloneqq\llbracket kd^{2}+k-1\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\coloneqq\llbracket kd^{2}+k-1\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math>, composed of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint blocks each of size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{2}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{2}+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote the <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th block by <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{i}\coloneqq\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}+x\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}x\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{i}\coloneqq\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}+x\mathrel{\mathop{\mathchar 58\relax}}x\in\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> be the class of binary-valued functions on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket kd^{2}+k-1\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket kd^{2}+k-1\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The </span><math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> function.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All functions </span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> that equal </span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> precisely on a size-</span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> subset of </span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{i}\backslash\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{i}\backslash\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (we exclude the first coordinate) for some </span><math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that this only requires shattering a set of size at most <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, define distributions <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\dots,P_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\dots,P_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\times\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\times\mathinner{\left\{0,1\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math> with marginal PMFs</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{i}\mathinner{\left(X=x\right)}=\begin{cases}1-2d\epsilon,&amp;x=\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}\\
2\epsilon/d,&amp;x\in\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}+1,\dots,i\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}-1\right\}}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{i}\mathinner{\left(X=x\right)}=\begin{cases}1-2d\epsilon,&amp;x=\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}\\
2\epsilon/d,&amp;x\in\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}+1,\dots,i\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}-1\right\}}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and label noise</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{i}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}=\frac{1}{4}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X},i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{i}\mathinner{\left(f^{*}\mathinner{\left(X\right)}\neq Y|X=x\right)}=\frac{1}{4}\quad\forall x\in\mathcal{X},i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some unknown <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Any (<a href="#S4.Ex46" title="Equation MSHT ‣ 4.3 Multi-Distribution SHT ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">MSHT</span></a>) algorithm <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, with confidence parameter <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, that tests the functions <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}=\dots=f_{k}=f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}=\dots=f_{k}=f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on this instance requires a sample size of</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{\mathcal{A}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,0.01\right)}\geq\frac{0.015kd}{2\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.015</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{\mathcal{A}}\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,0.01\right)}\geq\frac{0.015kd}{2\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem D.2. ‣ D.6 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the following hypotheses:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex136" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex136X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex136X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{$H_{0}$: $f^{*}=f_{0}$.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext>: </mtext><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{$H_{0}$: $f^{*}=f_{0}$.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex136Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex136Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{$H_{1}$: $f^{*}$ equals $1$ precisely on a size-$d$ subset of $\mathcal{X}_{i}\backslash\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}\right\}}$ for some $i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}$.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mtext>: </mtext><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mtext> equals </mtext><mn>1</mn><mtext> precisely on a size-</mtext><mi>d</mi><mtext> subset of </mtext><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext> for some </mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{$H_{1}$: $f^{*}$ equals $1$ precisely on a size-$d$ subset of $\mathcal{X}_{i}\backslash\mathinner{\left\{\mathinner{\left(i-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)}\right\}}$ for some $i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}$.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">As in the proof of <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4 (() lower bound). ‣ 4.2 () Lower Bound ‣ 4 Structured Hypothesis Testing ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, we note that</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f_{i};P_{i}\right)}=1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f_{i};P_{i}\right)}=1/4</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A4.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and distribution <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f_{i};P_{i}\right)}=1/4+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f_{i};P_{i}\right)}=1/4+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\err\mathinner{\left(f_{j};P_{j}\right)}=1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>err</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\err\mathinner{\left(f_{j};P_{j}\right)}=1/4</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A4.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> must be able to distinguish both hypotheses. Define <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the number of times that <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled, which is a random quantity since the algorithm can be adaptive. Let <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the probability law under <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathinner{\left[k\right]}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will show, by contradiction, that <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}\gtrsim d/\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}\gtrsim d/\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> with constant probability under <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume to the contrary that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}\leq\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\geq 0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}\leq\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\geq 0.7</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We will construct an (<a href="#A4.Ex109" title="Equation SHT-Base ‣ Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">SHT-Base</span></a>) algorithm <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> by simulating <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that we are given sample access to a distribution <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> according to one of the (<a href="#A4.Ex109" title="Equation SHT-Base ‣ Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">SHT-Base</span></a>) hypotheses. Let <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{X}=\mathinner{\left(1-2d\epsilon,2\epsilon/d,\dots,2\epsilon/d\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{X}=\mathinner{\left(1-2d\epsilon,2\epsilon/d,\dots,2\epsilon/d\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the PMF over <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket d^{2}\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> (with <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> scaled by <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>). Consider the following strategy:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Run <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> on parameters <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,\delta\right)}=\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,0.1\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,\delta\right)}=\mathinner{\left(\epsilon,0.1\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. When it samples distribution <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<ul id="A4.I5.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=i</annotation></semantics></math>, sample <math id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}\sim P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(X,Y\right)}\sim P</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, sample <math id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim p_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim p_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\Ber\mathinner{\left(1/4\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\Ber\mathinner{\left(1/4\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A4.I5.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Return the data point <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathinner{\left(X+\mathinner{\left(j-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)},Y\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathinner{\left(X+\mathinner{\left(j-1\right)}\mathinner{\left(d^{2}+1\right)},Y\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The shift on <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that it lives in <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, we set <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> outside of <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the unknown (<a href="#A4.Ex109" title="Equation SHT-Base ‣ Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">SHT-Base</span></a>) instance. Hence, <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I5.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in both coincide.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We terminate whenever the first of the following occurs:</p>
<ul id="A4.I5.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> has sampled distribution <math id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> more than <math id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> times, output <math id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{YES}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{YES}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.24</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> terminates, output <math id="A4.I5.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{D}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{D}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.SS6.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS6.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that this process requires at most <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}+1\leq\frac{0.3d}{2\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}+1\leq\frac{0.3d}{2\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 8\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 8\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption) samples from <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, which beats the lower bound of <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1. ‣ D.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs of ‣ Is Multi-Distribution Learning as Easy as PAC Learning: Sharp Rates with Bounded Label Noise" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. Nevertheless, under the chosen parameters, <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> indeed succeeds. In what follows, we use <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the probability law under <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. When the probability does not depend on the instance, we drop the subscript. Next, we analyze the output of <math id="A4.SS6.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> under each hypothesis.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline"><math id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{H_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑯</mi><mn>𝟎</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{H_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>:</h4>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that the null hypothesis <math id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is true. Then,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\left\{T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right\}}\cap\mathinner{\left\{\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\right\}}\right)}+\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\left\{T_{i}\leq\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right\}}\cap\mathinner{\left\{\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right\}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>𝖣</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\left\{T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right\}}\cap\mathinner{\left\{\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\right\}}\right)}+\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\left\{T_{i}\leq\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right\}}\cap\mathinner{\left\{\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right\}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\middle|T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\middle|T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 56.9055pt+\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}-\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\left\{T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right\}}\cap\mathinner{\left\{\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right\}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>𝖣</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 56.9055pt+\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}-\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathinner{\left\{T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right\}}\cap\mathinner{\left\{\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right\}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\middle|T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}+\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}-\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{YES}\middle|T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}+\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}-\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}-\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{NO}\middle|T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖸𝖤𝖲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖭𝖮</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.05</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(\mathsf{D}_{i}=\mathsf{YES}\right)}-\mathbb{P}_{0}\mathinner{\left(T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}\mathbb{P}\mathinner{\left(\mathcal{A}_{s}=\mathsf{NO}\middle|T_{i}&gt;\frac{0.05d}{2\epsilon}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 0.99-0.3\cdot 0.76" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0.99</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0.76</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 0.99-0.3\cdot 0.76</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
